Built-in catalog data
---------------------
The files in crates/ballistics-store/catalog/ hold calibers, bullets,
scopes, reticles, targets and animal drawings.

  * Bullet, ammunition and scope figures are factual specifications compiled
    from the manufacturers' published product information (and, for a few
    entries, retailers' pages). Each entry names its source. Facts like
    these belong to no one; they are given as found, without warranty.
  * Reticle drawings are the project's own. Each is built by the project's
    own code from the subtension figures the maker publishes (spacings, line
    widths, hold-point positions), with the layout read from the maker's
    published picture; none is traced or copied from the makers' artwork.
    Each entry names its source and says which values were published and
    which were measured from the picture.
  * Animal drawings are the project's own.
  * ISSF target dimensions follow the ISSF rules. The game guideline values
    (vital zones, minimum energies, sizes) are the project's own estimates;
    the Swedish ammunition classes summarise Naturvårdsverket's rules
    (NFS 2023:8), which are public law. Check the current rules.

The project's own parts of the catalog (the drawings, notes and guideline
values) are licensed under the same licences as the source code.

Product and company names (for example Kahles, Vortex, Swarovski Optik,
Zeiss, Meopta, GPO, Norma, Lapua, Hornady, Federal, Strelok Pro) and reticle
names (for example EBR-7C, Dead-Hold, SKMR4) are trademarks of their owners. They are used only to
identify the products. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by
any of them.

The Strelok Pro importer reads backup files for interoperability. It
contains no Strelok code or data.

No warranty
-----------
Ballistic predictions are estimates. Always confirm your rifle's point of
impact on paper at real distances before hunting, and follow your country's
hunting laws.
